Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(voice): the call opens first, then the phrase is said
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A wake that produced only a text reply was a send that ran before the page was pushed and
threw, so openChatCall never ran — in a call there is no typing, which is how the report
read. The page is pushed first now, and the phrase is sent afterwards with both the
utterance read and the send itself guarded: the call opens no matter what they do.

Also in this commit: 唤醒后开新对话 or 接着上次 — one setting, honoured by the wake word and
the AI key alike (a plain tap on 通话 keeps the conversation on screen).
---
 app/lib/ui/chat/chat_screen.dart | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 app/lib/voice/wake_settings.dart | 20 +++++++++----
 2 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/lib/ui/chat/chat_screen.dart b/app/lib/ui/chat/chat_screen.dart
index 18aefb4..47cee06 100644
--- a/app/lib/ui/chat/chat_screen.dart
+++ b/app/lib/ui/chat/chat_screen.dart
@@ -1518,27 +1518,23 @@ class _ChatScreenState extends ConsumerState<ChatScreen> with WidgetsBindingObse
       return;
     }
